WEBVTT

00:00:03.916 --> 00:00:05.750
Yeah, that's probably best
for everybody.

00:00:05.916 --> 00:00:08.083
[Dave] Hey! Who let you out?
Get back in there!

00:00:08.250 --> 00:00:09.708
-Oh, boy.
-What are we gonna do?

00:00:09.875 --> 00:00:10.916
Oh, disgusted one,

00:00:11.625 --> 00:00:15.833
as you once believed in me,
I will now believe in myself.

00:00:15.916 --> 00:00:16.916
[sword clatters]

00:00:17.666 --> 00:00:18.666
[guards gasp]

00:00:19.583 --> 00:00:21.208
Huh?

00:00:21.291 --> 00:00:22.708
-Wait. What?
-[all laughing]

00:00:25.750 --> 00:00:27.083
-[groans]
-Ooh!

00:00:27.166 --> 00:00:28.541
[screams, grunts]

00:00:29.833 --> 00:00:31.000
[groans, grunts]

00:00:31.583 --> 00:00:34.500
Whoa! What's happening? Whoa!

00:00:34.583 --> 00:00:35.583
-[Sadness gasps]
-[Anger laughing]

00:00:35.791 --> 00:00:36.875
[groaning]

00:00:37.916 --> 00:00:38.916
No...

00:00:39.083 --> 00:00:40.083
Dave, help! Help!

00:00:40.250 --> 00:00:41.250
Hold on!

00:00:41.750 --> 00:00:42.750
[cop] Dave!

00:00:44.708 --> 00:00:45.958
Lance!

00:00:46.125 --> 00:00:47.125
[Lance] Goodbye, friends.

00:00:47.291 --> 00:00:48.916
Hello, destiny!

00:00:49.666 --> 00:00:51.000
Well, there's a lid
for every pot.

00:00:51.166 --> 00:00:52.166
Come on!

00:00:54.041 --> 00:00:55.333
[Fear] What do we do?
What do we do?

00:00:55.500 --> 00:00:57.291
Whoa, Anger, stop.
Where are you going?

00:00:57.458 --> 00:01:00.041
Um, back to Headquarters,
to help Riley!

00:01:00.208 --> 00:01:01.541
Riley's not up there.

00:01:01.708 --> 00:01:03.166
She's out there.

00:01:03.333 --> 00:01:06.041
We can't go back
without her Sense of Self.

00:01:06.208 --> 00:01:09.375
You want us to go all the way
to the Back of the Mind?

00:01:09.541 --> 00:01:11.458
Are you out of your mind?

00:01:11.625 --> 00:01:12.875
But, Joy, how will we...

00:01:13.041 --> 00:01:14.041
-[male cop] Freeze!
-Come on!

00:01:14.208 --> 00:01:15.208
[male cop] Hold it right there!

00:01:15.291 --> 00:01:16.291
[siren wailing]

00:01:16.791 --> 00:01:19.875
[scoffs] How do we get there?
Do you even have a plan, Joy?

00:01:20.041 --> 00:01:22.583
I bet Anxiety would have
a really good plan...

00:01:22.750 --> 00:01:24.541
Of course I have a plan.
Who doesn't have a plan?

00:01:24.708 --> 00:01:27.000
Look, she's not the only one
who can project the future.

00:01:27.166 --> 00:01:30.208
First, all we have to do is,
uh...

00:01:30.541 --> 00:01:31.541
Give me a second.

00:01:32.083 --> 00:01:34.541
Ooh! Follow the stream
of consciousness,

00:01:34.708 --> 00:01:36.291
and then we take
a nice, easy float

00:01:36.375 --> 00:01:37.583
all the way
to the Back of the Mind.

00:01:37.666 --> 00:01:38.916
[Fear] Where all
the bad memories are.

00:01:39.000 --> 00:01:40.000
[Joy] Exactly. And there,

00:01:40.083 --> 00:01:42.458
we'll find the Riley
we know and love.

00:01:43.041 --> 00:01:44.666
We'll put her
Sense of Self back,

00:01:44.750 --> 00:01:46.666
and then Riley
will be Riley again.

00:01:46.750 --> 00:01:47.750
[Fear] Okay,
I'm gonna give it to you.

00:01:47.833 --> 00:01:49.000
That could actually work.

00:01:49.083 --> 00:01:50.166
[Joy] Yeah, it could!

00:01:50.250 --> 00:01:54.375
And then I tell Anxiety, "Hey,
don't worry so much anymore."

00:01:54.541 --> 00:01:56.750
And she'll say,
"Wow, Joy, I never thought

00:01:56.833 --> 00:01:58.250
"of that before. Thank you."

00:01:58.333 --> 00:01:59.625
And then we hug
and become best friends...

00:01:59.791 --> 00:02:01.541
[Anger] And then I punt her
into the dump.

00:02:02.375 --> 00:02:03.458
-[Anxiety screaming]
-What? No, Anger.

00:02:03.541 --> 00:02:05.458
Okay, fine. No punting.

00:02:06.875 --> 00:02:08.875
Don't worry, I know
right where the stream is.

00:02:09.041 --> 00:02:11.458
Sadness and I
have been here before. Oh.

00:02:11.541 --> 00:02:13.500
[Disgust]
Joy, this is a dead end.

00:02:13.666 --> 00:02:15.958
Those are the worst kinds
of ends!

00:02:16.125 --> 00:02:19.583
Everything's changing so fast!
[crying]

00:02:19.666 --> 00:02:20.916
So, we're lost.

00:02:21.000 --> 00:02:23.416
No. You're never lost
if you're having fun.

00:02:23.500 --> 00:02:24.750
No one is having fun, Joy.

00:02:24.833 --> 00:02:26.541
Oh, come on! Look at Sadness.

00:02:26.625 --> 00:02:28.000
She's having a great time.

00:02:28.083 --> 00:02:29.500
[crying]

00:02:29.583 --> 00:02:31.083
I thought you knew
where you were going.

00:02:31.250 --> 00:02:32.250
I do. I did.

00:02:32.333 --> 00:02:33.875
-I just need a moment.
-She doesn't know.

00:02:34.041 --> 00:02:35.333
We're stuck here!

00:02:36.291 --> 00:02:38.083
Oh, Riley's awake.

00:02:38.250 --> 00:02:40.500
Wait, she's up too early.
What are they doing to her?

00:02:40.791 --> 00:02:42.541
Come on,
we'll find another way.

00:02:44.083 --> 00:02:46.208
Don't worry, Riley.
We're coming.

00:02:48.083 --> 00:02:49.708
[memories clinking]

00:02:49.791 --> 00:02:50.958
[breathing heavily]

00:02:52.125 --> 00:02:53.208
[Ennui sighs]

00:02:53.291 --> 00:02:55.416
Why are we up so early?

00:02:55.583 --> 00:02:57.833
Because, mon ami,
we need to speed things up,

00:02:58.000 --> 00:02:59.333
and that means
we hit the ice early,

00:02:59.500 --> 00:03:02.125
and practice like
we've never practiced before.

00:03:02.291 --> 00:03:03.833
[Ennui] Aren't we already good
at hockey?

00:03:04.000 --> 00:03:05.000
[Envy] We're good.

00:03:05.083 --> 00:03:07.541
-But the Fire Hawks are great.
-That's right!

00:03:08.958 --> 00:03:10.708
[grunts, groans]

00:03:11.291 --> 00:03:12.291
[Anxiety]
Every time we miss,

00:03:12.375 --> 00:03:13.625
we skate a lap
around the rink.

00:03:13.708 --> 00:03:15.666
Hockey is not a game,
it is a sport.

00:03:15.750 --> 00:03:17.416
[Riley grunts]

00:03:25.375 --> 00:03:27.000
[grunts]

00:03:27.083 --> 00:03:28.541
-Yes!
-[Envy] Wow.

00:03:28.875 --> 00:03:30.125
That was amazing.

00:03:30.208 --> 00:03:32.208
We need to be that good
every time.

00:03:32.291 --> 00:03:33.375
Let's run it again.

00:03:33.458 --> 00:03:35.541
Hey, I see I'm not the only
one who likes to start early.

00:03:35.625 --> 00:03:36.625
[Anxiety] You guys, it's Val!

00:03:36.833 --> 00:03:38.083
We had the same idea.

00:03:38.166 --> 00:03:39.541
We're basically
the same person.

00:03:39.625 --> 00:03:40.875
We're gonna be best friends.

00:03:41.041 --> 00:03:42.416
How long have you been here?

00:03:42.583 --> 00:03:44.375
I don't know. Maybe an hour.

00:03:44.541 --> 00:03:46.791
I just wanted to get in
some extra ice time.

00:03:46.958 --> 00:03:48.083
I'm the same way.

00:03:48.166 --> 00:03:49.833
[Anxiety]
Oh, my gosh. She gets us.

00:03:49.916 --> 00:03:52.083
See? I told the other girls
you'd figure it out.

00:03:52.166 --> 00:03:54.250
You get what it takes
to be the best.

00:03:56.625 --> 00:03:57.708
Look at us.

00:03:57.875 --> 00:03:59.625
This is going great!

00:03:59.708 --> 00:04:02.166
Yeah! But we need Val
to really like us.

00:04:02.250 --> 00:04:04.333
Oh, we should ask Val
lots of questions.

00:04:04.500 --> 00:04:06.208
People love
talking about themselves.

00:04:06.375 --> 00:04:09.375
So, what was your freshman
year on the Fire Hawks like?

00:04:09.541 --> 00:04:12.125
I mean,
it was a lot of work,

00:04:12.291 --> 00:04:13.750
like, a lot... [chuckles]

00:04:13.916 --> 00:04:16.041
but it's also
how I met my best friends.

00:04:16.125 --> 00:04:18.166
Val is sharing things with us!

00:04:18.250 --> 00:04:20.375
Hey, a few of us are just
gonna hang out tonight,

00:04:20.541 --> 00:04:22.500
order some food.
You should come.

00:04:22.583 --> 00:04:24.875
Oh! An exclusive invitation.
[chuckles]

00:04:24.958 --> 00:04:25.958
We're going!

00:04:26.416 --> 00:04:27.583
-Really?
-Definitely.

00:04:27.750 --> 00:04:28.750
It'll be fun.

00:04:28.833 --> 00:04:30.625
[coach] All right, ladies,
let's warm up.

00:04:32.250 --> 00:04:33.250
Hey, Riley.

00:04:33.333 --> 00:04:34.333
Hi.

00:04:34.416 --> 00:04:36.541
We are not sharing Val
with them.

00:04:36.708 --> 00:04:38.458
[grunts] Early mornings
make me so hungry.

00:04:38.625 --> 00:04:39.708
I know, right?

00:04:40.000 --> 00:04:42.250
I'd give anything for a piece
of pizza right now.

00:04:42.333 --> 00:04:43.333
Yes!

00:04:43.500 --> 00:04:45.250
See? I told you I'd find it.

00:04:45.416 --> 00:04:46.791
The Stream of Consciousness.

00:04:46.958 --> 00:04:49.541
-[Sadness] But, Joy...
-Wow! Our girl is hungry.

00:04:49.750 --> 00:04:50.875
Hop on something delicious!

00:04:51.041 --> 00:04:52.375
-Joy...
-Ooh, deep dish.

00:04:52.458 --> 00:04:54.125
[chuckles]
And it's still warm.

00:04:54.291 --> 00:04:55.708
Extra cheese, baby!

00:04:55.791 --> 00:04:56.791
Sadness, come on.

00:04:56.875 --> 00:04:58.250
But I've been trying
to tell you.

00:04:58.416 --> 00:05:00.458
We can't take the tube back,
Joy.

00:05:00.791 --> 00:05:03.333
Someone has to be
at the console to recall us.

00:05:03.500 --> 00:05:05.458
She's right. We'd be stranded.

00:05:05.625 --> 00:05:06.958
Yeah. Anxiety would have
thought about that.

00:05:07.125 --> 00:05:08.416
Well, I doubt it. Fine.

00:05:08.583 --> 00:05:10.000
Okay. Uh...

00:05:10.333 --> 00:05:13.083
So, someone's gonna have to
crawl up that tube,

00:05:13.250 --> 00:05:14.500
and go back to Headquarters,

00:05:14.666 --> 00:05:16.375
and at the right moment,
bring us back.

00:05:16.458 --> 00:05:18.041
Oh, I'll do it.
I'll pound that...

00:05:18.208 --> 00:05:19.291
I don't think so, punty.

00:05:19.375 --> 00:05:21.125
-Okay, here's the thing.
-You were never an option.

00:05:21.208 --> 00:05:22.208
Thank you.

00:05:22.291 --> 00:05:24.458
You want me to crawl through
a tube in this?

00:05:24.625 --> 00:05:25.916
Yeah, not happening.

00:05:28.708 --> 00:05:31.541
[gasps] Oh, no, not me.

00:05:31.708 --> 00:05:33.416
Yes! Sadness, you could do it.

00:05:33.583 --> 00:05:35.708
You know the console
better than anybody.

00:05:35.875 --> 00:05:37.750
You've read the manuals
cover to cover.

00:05:37.916 --> 00:05:39.375
I mean, you say that,

00:05:39.458 --> 00:05:42.875
but I know a lot less about
Manual 28, Chapter Seven,

00:05:42.958 --> 00:05:44.625
"How to Recall
Non-Memory Objects"

00:05:44.708 --> 00:05:46.416
than most folks realize.

00:05:46.500 --> 00:05:48.083
You've proven my point
for me, Sadness.

00:05:48.166 --> 00:05:49.291
That sounds like a yes.

00:05:49.375 --> 00:05:50.375
[man on radio]
Where is everybody?

00:05:50.458 --> 00:05:51.458
You on break again?

00:05:51.541 --> 00:05:53.750
Ooh! Walkie-talkies. Here.
Check-check-check.

00:05:53.833 --> 00:05:55.041
Can you hear me?
I gotta press a button.

00:05:55.125 --> 00:05:57.541
Go for Joy. Copy that. Over.
Oh, I love 'em!

00:05:57.625 --> 00:05:58.791
We'll signal you
when we get there,

00:05:58.958 --> 00:06:00.916
-and then you bring us back.
-Oh...

00:06:01.000 --> 00:06:03.041
[Joy] Sadness, it's the fastest
way back to Headquarters.

00:06:03.125 --> 00:06:04.208
Joy, I can't do it.

00:06:04.291 --> 00:06:06.625
I'm not strong like you are.

00:06:06.708 --> 00:06:08.166
I know you, Sadness.

00:06:08.250 --> 00:06:09.875
You are strong.

00:06:09.958 --> 00:06:12.625
I can't give you
specific examples right now,

00:06:12.791 --> 00:06:14.166
but you got this.

00:06:15.541 --> 00:06:16.541
-[Joy grunts]
-[Sadness whimpers]

00:06:16.625 --> 00:06:18.583
Just don't look down
and keep moving.

00:06:18.666 --> 00:06:20.250
[Sadness] Yeah, I can do it.

00:06:20.333 --> 00:06:21.916
[crying hysterically]

00:06:23.375 --> 00:06:24.958
She'll be okay. Right?

00:06:25.041 --> 00:06:26.500
Uh, fifty-fifty.

00:06:26.833 --> 00:06:28.750
Mmm! You want one?

00:06:29.875 --> 00:06:31.041
But we hate those things.

00:06:31.125 --> 00:06:32.875
They taste like cardboard.

00:06:32.958 --> 00:06:35.208
-[Embarrassment groaning]
-We can't say no to Val.

00:06:35.291 --> 00:06:37.166
Okay, no, you're so right.

00:06:37.250 --> 00:06:38.625
We eat whatever Val eats.

00:06:38.708 --> 00:06:40.125
-That's the spirit!
-Whoo!

00:06:40.333 --> 00:06:42.500
Envy, I think you're really
in the zone.

00:06:42.666 --> 00:06:43.958
Take the wheel,
I'll be right back.

00:06:44.125 --> 00:06:45.791
She picked me! She picked me.
Did you see that, Ennui?

00:06:45.875 --> 00:06:46.875
She picked me.

00:06:46.958 --> 00:06:48.708
You care too much
about things.

00:06:48.875 --> 00:06:51.000
Mmm. Mmm-hmm.

00:06:51.416 --> 00:06:54.083
It's got
a very interesting texture.

00:06:54.166 --> 00:06:55.833
It tastes like... Mmm...

00:06:56.708 --> 00:06:58.541
What does it remind me of?
Um...

00:06:59.750 --> 00:07:03.166
Cardboard? Asparagus?
Broccoli?

00:07:03.250 --> 00:07:04.833
What are they doing to her
up there?

00:07:05.000 --> 00:07:06.500
I don't know,
but we have to go.

00:07:06.583 --> 00:07:07.791
No! No way am I step...

00:07:07.875 --> 00:07:10.458
-We have to. Riley needs us.
-[groans]

00:07:10.541 --> 00:07:11.666
Okay, fine!

00:07:11.750 --> 00:07:13.708
Ugh. Ew! Ew!

00:07:13.791 --> 00:07:15.000
-[Fear whimpering]
-[Joy grunts]

00:07:15.083 --> 00:07:17.375
Gross.
I think I'm gonna be sick.

00:07:18.291 --> 00:07:20.291
[♪ dramatic music playing]

00:07:24.000 --> 00:07:25.333
[crackling]

